{
  "_comment": "THE ISO/IEC 1989:2002 8.9 RESERVED WORD LIST (kb/Work PB4297), transcribed from the post-ballot text ISO/IEC 1989:2002(E) of 2001-12-04 (P2 of kb/Work PB3602 'Sources': the register's durable copy fcd/v200112/cobolv200112.pdf, 8.9 on its printed pages 141-143). The words are facts; no text of the standard is held. scripts/gen-reserved-words.ps1 reads this file for the r2002 flag of tests/version-matrix/reserved-words.json and ReservedWords.Table.cs: the 2002 standard's own list, which outranks GnuCOBOL's cobol2002.words (CLAUDE.md rule 1); the generator adds ALIGNED, which 8.9 omits although Annex F.1 item 6 lists it among the reserved words 2002 added and 13.16.1 defines its clause. ReservedWordsDriftTests holds this file to the generated table. CONTENT-FILTER RULE: never print this file into a conversation. The second list, addedByAnnexF1, is the same text's Annex F.1 item 6 (\"The following reserved words have been added\", printed page 835): the words 2002 reserved that the previous standard did not, alphanumeric words only (its '>>', '*>', '&' and '::' are not words of the 8.9 list), with the printed GROUUP-USAGE read as GROUP-USAGE. An 8.9 word that list does not name was already reserved at 1985, which scripts/gen-reserved-words.ps1 asserts of the 85 flag (kb/Work PB3957).",
